Z||000004||Fierowrecker||10-14-2001||12:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLAMMED87GT:<BR><B><BR>I was washing my Fiero and once again saw this car. It's an early Mitsubishi Eclipse. They have that wrap around style wing on them from the factory. Well, this guy has that along with a crappy GTS wing mounted on top of it!!!!! It's ridiculous! Some of you might remember at Dells 2000 when a few of us were hanging out in the parking lot talking and this guy drives by with a new camaro with the same deal. He had the stock wrap around wing and a "rice" type wing mounted on top of it. It looked so silly!!!<P>Why? Maybe it looks good in their opinion. I'll stay with my stock wing and 7" stands!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just for grins, tape some tufts of yarn to the top and back of most wings on cars, and you will notice they don't move while the car is in motion, as they are out of the airflow...<BR>Tell the ricers the tufts of yarn are to help stabilize the vorticies of air off the wing and improve the drag coefficency...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
